### 4.2 LLM Simulation

We evaluated four instruction-tuned models:
- GPT-4o, accessed via API;
- Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct;
- Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct;
- Mistral-Large-Instruct-2407.

The most pressing directions for future work follow from these restrictions:

- synthesizing text with the resource-poor language as the matrix language, e.g., through the reverse-direction pipeline outlined in Section 6.8;
- evaluating on code-switched data from other domains;
- measuring sensitivity to MT quality;
- sampling romanizations from community-specific spelling distributions;
- accounting for the pragmatic functions of switching in label transfer.

